# Contact form delivery, via EmailJS (emailjs.com).
#
# All three values come from your EmailJS dashboard. The public key is
# designed to be exposed in client-side code — that's how EmailJS works, there
# is no server to hide it behind — so shipping it in the browser bundle is
# expected, not a leak.
#
#   VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID   Email > your service > Service ID
#   VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID  Email Templates > your template > Template ID
#   VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY   Account > General > Public Key
#
# Your EmailJS template should reference these variables:
#   {{from_name}} {{from_email}} {{reply_to}} {{company}} {{project_type}}
#   {{budget}} {{message}} {{subject}}
# Set the template's "To Email" directly in the EmailJS dashboard (not passed
# from here) so it can't be redirected by a form submission.
#
# Leave any of the three unset and the form will say so plainly and fall back
# to opening a prefilled email instead — the same fallback also covers a
# genuine send failure. It never silently discards a message.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Clinic demo assistant (/work/clinic), via the Gemini API free tier.
#
# SERVER-ONLY: no VITE_ prefix, so Vite never puts these in the browser
# bundle. They're read by api/chat.ts — on Vercel set them under Project >
# Settings > Environment Variables; locally, put them in .env.local and
# `npm run dev` serves /api/chat for you.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY  Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com) > Get API key
#   GEMINI_MODEL    Optional. Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash-lite.
#
# Leave the key unset and the assistant still works, answering from the
# clinic's scripted FAQ. It also falls back to those answers when Gemini
# returns a rate-limit or quota error, times out, or the visitor goes over
# the per-IP limit (8 a minute, 40 a day).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=

# Public URL of the site, with no trailing slash. Drives the canonical tag,
# og:url, og:image, robots.txt and sitemap.xml — change it here when moving to
# a custom domain, nothing else. Defaults to https://tn-digital-designs.vercel.app
# when empty (see vite.config.ts). Set it in Vercel's env vars too.
VITE_SITE_URL=
